==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*skrīþaną}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*(s)kreyt-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||twist, turn, bend}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|skrīthan}}, {{cog|dum|schriden}} ({{cog|nl|schrijden}}), {{cog|goh|skrītan}} ({{cog|de|schreiten}}), {{cog|non|skríða}} ({{cog|sv|skrida}}). The Indo-European root also gave Latin {{m|la|crīsō|crīsāre}} and Middle Irish {{m|mga|crith}} (Breton {{m|br|skrija||tremble with fear}}).

